When two pages have an identical layout, but contain fields of equal size with 
visible differences the display is coherent, and the changes will be shown in  
highlighted mode.                                                              
                                                                                                                                               
If fan-fold paper is being used ensure that the top of form is correctly set,  
as VIEWTEXT will print a header with the current date and then the recorded    
date and string of the      
If there is ANY difference in the pages a flag is set which can be used by the 
RUN COMMAND function (see section 4 of the User Guide) to save any page which  
has changed. When the comparison is completed, pressing ESCAPE twice will      
retur page(s). Pages are printed side by side, and therefore a
single printer page will contain up to 4 VIEWTEXT pages. When 4 pages have been
printed, a FORM FEED is sent to align the next sheet.                          
                                   n to the MAIN MENU. If the pages are then displayed (function 10) the     
highlights will have been removed. The highlights cannot be saved on disc, nor 
will they be printed.                                                          
                                                              
All graphics characters are replaced by "*" characters when printing unless a  
MICROLINE 80 series or compatible printer is connected. During the print       
operation the prompt line displays a "WAIT" mess                                                             
PRINT PAGES - function 14 of the MAIN MENU prints the displayed pages. Note    
that a page must be displayed before it can be printed, as the display routine 
is used to load the printer bufage. At the end of each print  
the MAIN MENU is restored. For details of printer selection see section 5 of   
the User Guide (CONFIGURATION MENU).                                           
                                                             fers with a formatted page. If both pages are   
blank, or either page is present but has not been displayed an error message is
displayed inviting the user to display before attempting to print.             
