                                TRANSMIT FILE                                  
                                                                               
Function 15 of the MAIN ME--
The printer must be on and ready to receive characters, as function 14 will    
"hang" until the print operation is completed. Some CP/M systems will time the 
printer out, but this depends on the system and not on VIEWTEXT.               
         NU allows the user to send a pre-prepared message to 
the modem (if on-line) in addition to keyboard characters. The CONFIGURATION   
MENU (see section 5 of the User Guide) allows certain straps to be set or      
cleared which affect the operation of TRANSMIT. If the modem is off-line an    
error message is displayed on the prompt line.                                 
                                                                               
The user is prompted for a file name and also to seld sent    
must therefore not contain "!" or "|" characters. In .FRM and .PGE modes       
the BELL code is sounded at the end of the transmit operation. A form can hold 
more than one "@....!" field. Each field can be separated by comments. It is   
aect the L or R screen on   
which the file is to be displayed. The file is then loaded to the selected     
screen buffer and displayed. The filename extension is then tested to determine
the type of transmit operation to be performed, and the file datalso possible to delay the transmission of each field by placing "*" characters
between fields. Each "*" will force a wait of 1 second before sending the next 
field. This allows time-sensitive operations to be performed. Within each field
a "\" characte is sent to   
the modem in the appropriate manner. At the end of the transmit operation a    
BELL code is sent to the terminal, and any special configuration-dependent     
characters are sent to the modem.                                             r will send a CR,LF and will also remove any trailing spaces.    
