FORMS MODE - If the extension is .FRM (a form), only those characters enclosed 
in "@" and "!" or "@" and "|" are sent. The "@" is not sent, and if the "!"    
character is used a HASH (5FH) is sent as a field delimiter. The fiel                                                                          
SPEED MODE - If the extension is .SPD (speed page) a prompt is displayed on the
last line of the selected screen. The prompt is "SELECT:" and the user enters a
number and then presses RETURN. The number corresponds to a speed page index   
number displayed in column 1 of the speed page, and the associated string      
between the "[" and "]" characters will be sent to the modem. The incoming page
will be displayed on the other                                
Valid speed selector digits are "0" to "9". Up to 10 page numbers can be held  
on a page, and can therefore be double line spaced to improve visibility.      
